# Spondon frontend config — copy to `.env` and adjust.
#
# Vite inlines these at BUILD time, not at runtime: every value here ends up in
# the shipped bundle and is readable by anyone who opens the page. Nothing that
# needs to stay secret belongs in this file.

# Base URL of the API. The default matches the backend's dev port (1184, the
# last four digits of student ID 23101184). In production this is the deployed
# API origin, e.g. https://spondon-api.onrender.com — and changing it needs a
# rebuild, not just a restart.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:1184

# Google Maps JavaScript API key — the City-Wide Radar's map. Optional: with no
# key the radar falls back to its built-in SVG diagram rather than showing a
# blank grey box, so leaving this unset degrades one view instead of breaking it.
#
# A Maps JS key is visible in page source by definition. Restrict it by HTTP
# referrer in the Google Cloud console — that restriction, not secrecy, is what
# protects it. Needs the Maps JavaScript API enabled and billing on.
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
